1248			def:concrete-paired-line-measurement, def:consistency,
1249			thm:qld-conditioned-polynomial-bound}
1250		This is a formalization-only construction theorem. Fix a polynomially small
1251		function $\delta_Q(\eps)$. There is a function
1252		$\delta_P(\eps,md/q)=\poly(\eps,md/q)$, in the corrected sum sense,
1253		such that for every projective strategy passing with error $\eps$ and
1254		every joint point family satisfying the conclusions of
1255		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-10} with error $\delta_Q(\eps)$, the concrete POVM
1256		\[
1257			T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}
1258			=\hat M^{(\mathrm{Line},X),\ell_X}_{f_X}
1259			 \hat M^{(\mathrm{Line},Z),\ell_Z}_{f_Z}
1260			 \hat M^{(\mathrm{Line},X),\ell_X}_{f_X}
1261		\]
1262		has evaluated consistency defect at most $\delta_P(\eps,md/q)$ with that
1263		joint point family, averaged over two independent line-point samples,
1264		for every directed opposite placement.
